# Variables

Hello, {% $user.name %}. Version {% $version %}.

## Highlighting

Each reference below should be colored as a variable from `$` to the end, including subscripts.

- Dotted path: {% $user.profile.email %}
- Index subscript: {% $user.roles[0].label %}
- String subscript: {% $user["profile"]["display-name"] %}
- Mixed: {% $user.roles[0]["id"] %}
- Frontmatter: {% $markdoc.frontmatter.author.links.github %}
- Undefined (should be an error): {% $markdoc.frontmatter.missing %}
- Function arguments: {% if equals($user.roles[0].id, "admin") %}Shown to admins.{% /if %}

{% callout type="note" title=$user.roles[0].label %}
The title of this callout is a variable with a subscript.
{% /callout %}

## Completion

Try these on the empty line at the end of this file (completion does not run inside code like the examples here):

- Type `{% $` to list variables: `user`, `flags`, `version`, `markdoc`, and `markdoc.frontmatter.*` for this page (`title`, `route`, `author`, `draft`).
- Type `{% $user.` to list `name`, `profile`, `roles`; then `{% $user.roles[0].` to list `id`, `label`.
- Type `{% $markdoc.` for `frontmatter`, then `{% $markdoc.frontmatter.author.` for `name`, `links`.
- Type `{% callout title=$` to complete a variable as an attribute value.
- Type `{% callout title=` to see function names (`uppercase`, `includes`, and the built-ins) after the enum values.
- Type `{% if ` to see function names, and `{% if equals(` or `{% if equals($flags.beta, ` for argument completion.
- Type `{% ` to see tag names first and function names below them; type `{% eq` to see only `equals`.
- Inside a string, e.g. `{% callout title="$`, no variables are suggested.

